<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bud Bagsak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moro-rebellion">Moro Rebellion</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bud Bagsak was fought in June 1913 on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolo">Jolo</a> in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> between American troops under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-j-pershing">John J. Pershing</a>, with Philippine Scouts, and several hundred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tausug">Tausug</a> fighters who had fortified the mountain. Several hundred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moro-people">Moros</a>, including women and children, were killed. It was the last major battle of the American campaign against the Moros, which ended armed resistance in Sulu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bud-bagsak.jpg" alt="Battle of Bud Bagsak" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DA Poster 21-48 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Knocking_Out_the_Moros._DA_Poster_21-48.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
